  "scope": "Separate kept-stack clone with one opt-in switch for the MTP draft's hidden-row state across context checkpoint restores. The draft pairs the first token of each prompt batch with the last hidden row of the previous target batch; the pinned engine does not save that row with a checkpoint, so after a restore the next batch pairs its first token with the row the previous request left. This engine saves the row and the last verification rows with every checkpoint, in the layout of llama.cpp PR 30141; GGML_M5_LAB_MTP_STATE=restore applies them on restore, as that PR does, and unset keeps the pinned behaviour. GGML_M5_LAB_MTP_STATE_TRACE=1 prints one M5_MTPSTATE line per save and per restore, with how far the row in use is from the saved one. Kernels, fusion, weights, arithmetic, loader, allocator, context policy and server code unchanged; diagnostic only, never a default.",
